---
module: plain_parser
func_id: find-config-file
---

***conformance tests***

# config-next-to-spec
With `project/config.yaml` holding `template-dir: template`, `plain-parser check project/top.plain` run from the parent of `project` prints the OK line.

# config-in-working-directory
With `config.yaml` holding `template-dir: project/template` in the working directory and none next to the module, `plain-parser check project/top.plain` prints the OK line.

# config-name-option
With the configuration in `project/web.config.yaml`, `plain-parser check project/top.plain --config-name web.config.yaml` prints the OK line, and without the option it exits with code 1.

# no-config
Without any config file, `plain-parser check project/top.plain` exits with code 1 and writes exactly `Error: Module does not exist (helper).` on standard error.

***acceptance tests***

# config-in-both-places
With a config file next to the module and another in the working directory, `plain-parser check project/top.plain` exits with code 2 and writes `found in two locations` on standard error; the same holds with `--template-dir`, and for `parse`, which writes nothing on standard output.

# unreadable-config
A config file holding `template-dir: [unclosed` makes `plain-parser check` exit with code 2 and write `Error reading config file` on standard error.
